From: Niluthon <37350260+Niluthon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 09:10:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/13] B70-0042: hot/cold cold-expert prefetch for prefill
 (B70_MOE_COLD_PREFETCH): double-buffered DMA into VRAM

Batches with at least B70_MOE_COLD_PREFETCH_MIN_TOKENS tokens (default 512) run the cold experts from one
of two VRAM slots instead of reading pinned host memory through UVA: layer L computes from one slot while
a copy stream DMAs layer L+1's cold experts into the other (events order the streams; the last layer
prefetches layer 0 for the next chunk). Same kernel, same bytes, so outputs are unchanged. Decode batches
(graph capture sizes <= 16) keep the UVA path. Costs two slots of one layer's cold experts (0.53 GiB per
card at 144 hot of 256). Measured on 2x B70, 136 hot, util 0.95: prefill 2,600 -> 3,950 tok/s.
---
